Rallypoint 0057: AI call-for-help RE leftovers (T1.3), from gamemd.exe FUN_00708080.
Builds on 0044 (not re-landed). Retail addresses:
 - victim +0x2DC is SlaveOwner (written only by SlaveManager FUN_006AF580 @0x6AF5D7/0x6AF68B/0x6AF701):
   @0x7085AD the VEHICLE pass skips every candidate when the victim has a slave master.
 - techno +0x2E4 is the Tank Bunker link (FUN_00459301, 0x4596E6, 0x459814), NOT cargo: loaded
   transports answer (0044 wrongly skipped them). No bunkers in this engine.
 - ArchiveTarget (+0x218) == victim: only a unit that answered its own call has it (@0x70871F stores
   the victim into each recruit; FUN_0070C610 SetArchive is called with 0 by Stop/move paths
   0x4C7448 / 0x4D99FC). Buildings never archive themselves (FUN_00455D50 stores a rally cell), so
   0044's building boost is removed. x100 infantry applies to negative values too (@0x708351), vehicle
   x10 only to positive (@0x7085B7/0x7085BB). Recruits' Area_Guard centre is the victim.
 - FUN_0056D100 / FUN_0056D230: MovementZone -1 -> ok; candidate cell outside the usable area -> ok;
   else zone id (cell -> zone block -> per-MovementZone id) of victim == candidate. Replaced the
   Amphibious-domain stand-in with pathfind::reach_mask (integer BFS under find_path_t's neighbour
   rules, one flood per domain/crusher). Not pinned: whether building-occupied cells share the zone
   of the ground around them; the clone seeds from the cells ringing the foundation.
Also: save v62 (UnitTgt::archive_self). Simulation change for AI call-for-help only; integer code only.

